        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[28:15]  Once he entered the city unexpectedly, without being recognized by the people. He found two men fighting; one was (a Hebrew) from his people, and the other was (an Egyptian) from his enemies. The one from his people called on him for help against his enemy. Moses punched him, killing him. He said, \"This is the work of the devil; he is an enemy, and a profound misleader.\"",
